@* CopyButton's Overview, written by hand after Badge's: copying fixed text, copying a field's value
   (each previewed in the modes it has), what happens without script or clipboard access, and its
   own words. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A copy button copies text to the clipboard for the user to paste somewhere else: an install command, an ID, an API key. A <Anchor Href="docs/components/code">Code</Anchor> block has one built in. Use a CopyButton for text that isn't in a Code block, such as a single line of code or a field.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Copy text</Heading>
<TextBlock>A copy button can copy a fixed value, such as a command shown beside it. Set <Code>Text</Code> to the value. By default it's a ghost icon button, so give it a <Code>Label</Code> that says what it copies; the label is its name for screen readers and its tooltip ("Copy" by default).</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="copy-button-command" />
<TextBlock>After a copy, the icon turns to a check for a moment, and screen readers hear "Copied". The button keeps its name.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Copy from a field</Heading>
<TextBlock>A copy button can copy what another element contains at the moment it's pressed, such as a field's value. Set <Code>For</Code> to the element's id. It copies an input's or a text area's value, or any other element's text. If you give the button content, such as "Copy", it shows the text after the icon and is named by it.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="copy-button-from-field" />
<List>
    <ListItem>Set exactly one of <Code>Text</Code> and <Code>For</Code>. With both, or neither, the button throws.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>The button shows its own icons, so it also throws on <Code>StartIcon</Code>, <Code>EndIcon</Code>, <Code>Loading</Code> and <Code>LoadingLabel</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>Variant</Code>, <Code>Accent</Code> and <Code>Size</Code> work as on a <Anchor Href="docs/components/button">Button</Anchor>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">With JavaScript off</Heading>
<TextBlock>Copying requires <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor>. With JavaScript off, the button isn't shown at all, from the first paint, and the text it would copy stays on the page for the user to select.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The browser allows copying only on a secure page: https, or localhost while you develop. Without clipboard access, the button stays as it was and nothing is announced.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>To set the tooltip, and the name of an icon-only button, set <Code>Label</Code> ("Copy" by default). To set the word announced after copying, set <Code>CopiedLabel</Code> ("Copied"). To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Code>dotnet add package IzzyBlazor</Code>
        <CopyButton Text="dotnet add package IzzyBlazor" Label="Copy the command" />

        @* Copies the field's value when pressed. *@
        <TextField id="api-key" Label="API key" @bind-Value="key" ReadOnly>
            <EndAddon><CopyButton For="api-key" Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline">Copy</CopyButton></EndAddon>
        </TextField>
        """;
}
